A||||2||sjp777||Koni's for 88 suspension||||5||
Z||000000||sjp777||04-19-2001||10:25 PM||||I'm getting ready to throw a set of Koni's on my 88GT. According the the Koni website, the rears are adjustable but the fronts are not. The fronts are the ones I wanted to be able to adjust. I wanted to go stiffer than stock due to the lowering springs. Anybody got these, and are they really one setting fits all?<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||gixxer||04-19-2001||10:42 PM||||The fronts are adjustable in rebound only by compressing the shock fully and turning the shaft.<BR>Most people like them full soft in front. <BR>If you use your bump stops, I'd suggest lopping about 3/4" to 1" off and shape them into a pyramid or cone.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||04-20-2001||06:34 AM||||even full soft is stiff<BR>koni's and eibachs <P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">  <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
